  "title": "Adding Registers",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "al5-l1",
      "title": "ADD and SUB",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "ADD r (10 000 rrr, or 2 0 r in octal) adds a register to A: ADD B is 200. SUB r (2 2 r) subtracts it: SUB B is 220.",
        "The result always lands in A. The carry flag catches overflow, just like with ADI.",
        "ADD M and SUB M (r = 6) use a byte from memory instead of a register. More about M in Unit 6."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "006   ; 000: MVI B",
          "036   ;      30",
          "016   ; 002: MVI C",
          "014   ;      12",
          "170   ; 004: MOV A,B",
          "201   ; 005: ADD C",
          "323   ; 006: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "221   ; 010: SUB C",
          "221   ; 011: SUB C",
          "323   ; 012: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 014: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○●○●○●○ = 42",
          "LEDS ○○○●○○●○ = 18"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
