    {
      "id": "al5-l2",
      "title": "Doubling",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "ADD A (207) adds A to itself, so it doubles A. Do it again and you have 4 times the value, then 8, then 16.",
        "That's how simple processors multiply by 2, 4, 8 … very fast.",
        "Watch out: doubling 128 or more overflows past 255."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "076   ; 000: MVI A",
          "003   ;      3",
          "207   ; 002: ADD A",
          "323   ; 003: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "207   ; 005: ADD A",
          "323   ; 006: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "207   ; 010: ADD A",
          "323   ; 011: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 013: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○○○●●○ = 6",
          "LEDS ○○○○●●○○ = 12",
          "LEDS ○○○●●○○○ = 24"
        ]
      },
