    {
      "id": "al5-l3",
      "title": "Multiplying by Adding",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "The 8080 has no multiply instruction. But 13 × 10 is 13 × 8 + 13 × 2, and those are just doublings.",
        "Keep a copy of the number in another register: double A, save the ×2 in B, double twice more for ×8, then ADD B.",
        "Programmers in 1975 spent a lot of time on tricks like this."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "076   ; 000: MVI A",
          "015   ;      13",
          "207   ; 002: ADD A",
          "107   ; 003: MOV B,A",
          "207   ; 004: ADD A",
          "207   ; 005: ADD A",
          "200   ; 006: ADD B",
          "323   ; 007: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 011: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ●○○○○○●○ = 130"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
